THOUGHT: gameWindow is declared @Nullable and is set to a new GameWindow() in one place and to null in another, while window() returns it as non-null, causing the RETURN_NULLABLE error. To fix this without changing the public API, I can make window() defensively create a GameWindow if it’s null, ensuring it never returns null and leaving the field nullable for other internal uses. I’ll update the method accordingly and then run the build to verify that the NullAway error count decreases by one and no new errors are introduced.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/litiengine && sed -i '265,272s/public static GameWindow window() {.*/public static GameWindow window() {
    if (gameWindow == null) {
      gameWindow = new GameWindow();
    }
    return gameWindow;
  }/' src/de/gurkenlabs/litiengine/Game.java && ./gradlew compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1
```

